# SPDX-License-Identifier: CC-BY-4.0
# Citation metadata (Citation File Format 1.2.0). Minimal by design.
# P21.5 (ADR-067) wires the Zenodo deposit: `sig-exports deposit` uploads this file with
# each release and records the DOIs in docs/build/DEPOSITS.md. The `doi` / `identifiers`
# concept-DOI field is added below ONLY once a real *production* deposit exists — a
# sandbox `10.5072/…` DOI is not citable and must never be recorded here (RISK-P21-08,
# §3.1: no synthetic certainty). Until then the deposit is `gate pending: HG-07`.
#
# identifiers:
#   - type: doi
#     value: "10.5281/zenodo.<CONCEPT>"   # filled from DEPOSITS.md after the production deposit
#     description: "The concept DOI (all versions)"
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use SIG, please cite it using these metadata."
title: "SIG — Surveillance Infrastructure Graph"
abstract: >-
  An open, vendor-agnostic, temporally versioned, claim-level-provenance knowledge
  graph of surveillance infrastructure that federates public-interest datasets and
  primary records, with explicit evidence, contradiction, and coverage semantics.
type: software
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-09-09"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/SteveVitali/Eleutheria"
authors:
  - name: "The SIG project"
keywords:
  - surveillance
  - knowledge-graph
  - provenance
  - transparency
  - accountability
